@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### ==========================================================
### DAY 05-06: auth (register/login/logout) + session protected by requireAuth (/me)
### ==========================================================

### Create an account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "name": "test",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Who's logged in (with the cookie)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### Log out
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

### Check we're logged out (401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

### Log back in with the right password
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Wrong password (401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "mauvaismotdepasse"
}

### Register again with a taken email (409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "name": "Autre",
  "password": "autremotdepasse"
}

### ==========================================================
### DAY 07: reading articles. You need some articles in the DB first, otherwise you just get an empty list:
### docker compose -f platform/docker-compose.yml exec backend npx tsx src/script_test.ts
### ==========================================================

### List all articles
# @name listArticles
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/explore

### Details of the first article from the list above
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{listArticles.response.body.$.0.id}}

### Id that doesn't exist (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/id-inexistant

### ==========================================================
### DAY 08: create / edit / delete an article, with ownership check (isOwner). Needs two accounts (owner +
### intruder) - every register/login swaps the stored cookie for the account that just logged in.
### ==========================================================

### Create the "owner" account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "owner@example.com",
  "name": "Owner",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Create an article as the owner
# @name createArticle
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Mon article",
  "content": "Contenu de test"
}

### Edit your own article (200)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticle.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Mon article modifié",
  "content": "Nouveau contenu"
}

### Create the "intruder" account (replaces the current cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "intruder@example.com",
  "name": "Intruder",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Try to edit someone else's article (403)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticle.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Piratage",
  "content": "Piratage"
}

### Try to delete someone else's article (403)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticle.response.body.$.id}}

### Log back in as the owner
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "owner@example.com",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Delete your own article (204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticle.response.body.$.id}}

### Check the article is gone (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticle.response.body.$.id}}

### ==========================================================
### DAY 09: submit an article for review (DRAFT -> SUBMITTED)
### ==========================================================

### Create an account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "day9@example.com",
  "name": "Day9",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Create an article (DRAFT by default)
# @name createArticleDay9
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Article à soumettre",
  "content": "Contenu"
}

### Submit as the owner (200, status -> SUBMITTED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay9.response.body.$.id}}/submit

### Submit again (409, already SUBMITTED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay9.response.body.$.id}}/submit

### Create the "intruder" account (replaces the current cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "intruder9@example.com",
  "name": "Intruder9",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Try to submit someone else's article (403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay9.response.body.$.id}}/submit

### Submit an id that doesn't exist (404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/id-inexistant/submit

### ==========================================================
### DAY 10: reviews. An article has to be SUBMITTED to be reviewable,
### and you can't review your own article or the same one twice.
### ==========================================================

### Create the "author" account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "author10@example.com",
  "name": "Author10",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Create an article
# @name createArticleDay10
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Article à reviewer",
  "content": "Contenu"
}

### Submit it for review
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay10.response.body.$.id}}/submit

### Author tries to review their own article (403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay10.response.body.$.id}}/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "comment": "auto-review"
}

### Create the "reviewer" account (replaces the current cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "reviewer10@example.com",
  "name": "Reviewer10",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Review the article (201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay10.response.body.$.id}}/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "comment": "Bon article"
}

### Review it a second time (409)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay10.response.body.$.id}}/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "comment": "encore"
}

### List the article's reviews
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay10.response.body.$.id}}/reviews

### ==========================================================
### DAY 11: review decision (approve/reject) + PUBLISHED filter
### on public routes. A SUBMITTED article stays hidden publicly
### until a reviewer approves it, but its author and any
### potential reviewer can still see it
### (any logged-in account that isn't the author).
### ==========================================================

### Create the "author" account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "author11@example.com",
  "name": "Author11",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Create an article
# @name createArticleDay11
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Article à publier",
  "content": "Contenu"
}

### Submit it for review
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay11.response.body.$.id}}/submit

### Author (still logged in here) can see their own SUBMITTED (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay11.response.body.$.id}}

### Logged out, the article stays hidden (404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay11.response.body.$.id}}

### Create the "reviewer" account (replaces the current cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "reviewer11@example.com",
  "name": "Reviewer11",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### A logged-in third party (potential reviewer) can see the SUBMITTED too (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay11.response.body.$.id}}

### Review the article
# @name createReviewDay11
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay11.response.body.$.id}}/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "comment": "À valider"
}

### Log back in as the author (replaces the reviewer's cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "author11@example.com",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Author (not the reviewer) tries to decide (403)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/{{createReviewDay11.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "APPROVED"
}

### Log back in as the reviewer (replaces the author's cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "reviewer11@example.com",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Invalid decision (400)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/{{createReviewDay11.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "MAYBE"
}

### Approve the review (200, article -> PUBLISHED)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/{{createReviewDay11.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "APPROVED"
}

### Try to decide again (409)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/{{createReviewDay11.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "REJECTED"
}

### Article is now publicly visible (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay11.response.body.$.id}}

### It shows up in the public listing
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/explore

### ==========================================================
### DAY 12: comments. Only PUBLISHED articles
### can be commented. Only a comment's author can delete it.
### ==========================================================

### Create the "author" account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "author12@example.com",
  "name": "Author12",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Create an article
# @name createArticleDay12
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Article à commenter",
  "content": "Contenu"
}

### Submit it for review
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay12.response.body.$.id}}/submit

### Comment before it's published (404)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay12.response.body.$.id}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "Trop tôt"
}

### Create the "reviewer" account (replaces the current cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "reviewer12@example.com",
  "name": "Reviewer12",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Review the article
# @name createReviewDay12
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay12.response.body.$.id}}/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "comment": "ok"
}

### Approve (article -> PUBLISHED)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/reviews/{{createReviewDay12.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "decision": "APPROVED"
}

### Create the "commenter" account (replaces the current cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "commenter12@example.com",
  "name": "Commenter12",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Comment on the now published article (201)
# @name createCommentDay12
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay12.response.body.$.id}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "Super article"
}

### Log back in as the article's author (replaces the commenter's cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "author12@example.com",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Article author (not the comment's) tries to delete it (403)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/comments/{{createCommentDay12.response.body.$.id}}

### Log back in as the comment's author (replaces the author's cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "commenter12@example.com",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### The actual comment author deletes it (204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/comments/{{createCommentDay12.response.body.$.id}}

### Comment list should be empty
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay12.response.body.$.id}}/comments

### ==========================================================
### DAY 13: search/sort/pagination on GET /api/articles.
### Results depend on what articles you already have.
### ==========================================================

### Default listing (page 1, 10 per page, newest first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/explore

### Search (tweak the term to match an existing published title)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/explore?search=article

### Oldest to newest
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/explore?sort=oldest

### Pagination: 2 per page, page 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/explore?limit=2&page=1

### Pagination: 2 per page, page 2 (should differ from page 1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/explore?limit=2&page=2

### Guard rails: negative page -> bumped to 1, no error
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/explore?page=-5

### Guard rails: huge limit -> capped at 50, no error
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/explore?limit=99999

### ==========================================================
### DAY 14: Redis cache on the article listing. The HTTP response
### looks the same whether it comes from the cache or the DB.
### To actually check it works, hop into redis-cli:
### docker compose -f platform/docker-compose.yml exec redis redis-cli KEYS "articles:*"
### -> a GET should create an "articles:list:v0:..." key.
### -> creating/editing/deleting an article should bump
###    "articles:cache:version" from empty/0 to 1, and the next GET
###    should create a new "articles:list:v1:..." key.
### ==========================================================

### Warm up the cache (v0)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/explore

