### ==========================================================
### DAY 16: centralized error handling (safety net for
### unexpected errors)
### ==========================================================

### Triggers a real unhandled error (no body/Content-Type):
### 500 + a structured JSON log server-side (docker compose logs backend)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles

### ==========================================================
### DAY 17: basic security (helmet, rate limiting, locking down
### GET /:id/reviews).
###
### Helmet + global rate limiting can't be tested with a single
### request: check the security headers on any response above
### (Content-Security-Policy, X-Frame-Options,
### Strict-Transport-Security...), and to actually hit a 429,
### loop requests from a terminal:
###   for i in $(seq 1 12); do curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" \
###     -X POST http://localhost:4000/api/auth/login \
###     -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
###     -d '{"email":"nobody@test.com","password":"wrongpass"}'; done
### -> first 10: 401, from the 11th on: 429.
### The auth limiter skips successful attempts (skipSuccessfulRequests),
### so the same loop with the right password stays at 200.
### ==========================================================

### Create the "author" account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "author17@example.com",
  "name": "Author17",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Create an article
# @name createArticleDay17
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Article Day 17",
  "content": "Contenu pour tester la protection des reviews"
}

### Submit it for review
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay17.response.body.$.id}}/submit

### Create the "reviewer" account (replaces the current cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "reviewer17@example.com",
  "name": "Reviewer17",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Review the article
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay17.response.body.$.id}}/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "comment": "À valider"
}

### Reviewer checks the article's reviews (200, they're part of it)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay17.response.body.$.id}}/reviews

### Create a "third party" account (replaces the current cookie, neither author nor reviewer)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "stranger17@example.com",
  "name": "Stranger17",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Third party tries to read the reviews (403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay17.response.body.$.id}}/reviews

### Author logs back in (replaces the current cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "author17@example.com",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Author reads their article's reviews (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{createArticleDay17.response.body.$.id}}/reviews

### Author reads reviews of an article that doesn't exist (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/nonexistent-id-1234/reviews

