### ==========================================================
### DAY 19: file upload (multer + magic-bytes check via
### file-type + non-static storage + PUBLIC/PRIVATE access control
### via /api/uploads).
###
### Multipart uploads are a pain to script cleanly in
### .http (needs a binary file), so here's the reference curl
### from a terminal:
###
### curl -c cookies.txt -X POST http://localhost:4000/api/auth/register \
###   -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
###   -d '{"email":"upload19@test.com","name":"Upload19","password":"12345678"}'
###
### curl -b cookies.txt -X POST http://localhost:4000/api/uploads \
###   -F "file=@myimage.png;type=image/png"
### -> 201 { id, filename, originalName, mimeType, size, visibility: "PRIVATE", ownerId, createdAt }
###
### ==========================================================

### View a PRIVATE upload as the owner (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/uploads/REMPLACER_PAR_UN_ID_REEL

### Log out
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

### Same PRIVATE upload, logged out (403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/uploads/REMPLACER_PAR_UN_ID_REEL

### Upload that doesn't exist (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/uploads/id-inexistant

### Delete an upload without auth (401)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/uploads/REMPLACER_PAR_UN_ID_REEL

### ==========================================================
### DAY 20: profile + avatar (wraps up the User Management module with
### Day 21). Reuses the Day 19 upload system.
###
### Gotcha: if a Prisma field/relation "doesn't exist"
### even though the schema's right and the migration ran,
### "prisma migrate dev" doesn't always regenerate the client.
### If you get "Unknown argument" on a field that's definitely in
### schema.prisma -> docker compose exec backend npx prisma generate
### then restart the backend (tsx watch doesn't watch node_modules).
### ==========================================================

### Create an account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "day20@example.com",
  "name": "Day20",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### View your own profile (default avatar expected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me

### Edit your profile (200)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Day20 Renamed",
  "email": "day20-renamed@example.com"
}

### Create the "intruder" account (replaces the current cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "day20-intruder@example.com",
  "name": "Day20Intruder",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Intruder tries to grab the other account's email (409)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Peu importe",
  "email": "day20-renamed@example.com"
}

### View another account's PUBLIC profile (no email in the response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/REMPLACER_PAR_UN_ID_REEL

### Profile that doesn't exist (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/id-inexistant

### Set an upload as avatar (you need to upload a file
### via /api/uploads first, see Day 19 - swap the id below):
### 200, avatarUrl updated, and the upload flips to PUBLIC.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/users/me/avatar
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "uploadId": "REMPLACER_PAR_UN_ID_REEL"
}

### ==========================================================
### FRONT RECONCILIATION: GET /articles/submitted (review
### queue). Skips articles you wrote and the ones
### you already reviewed.
### ==========================================================

### Create the "author" account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "queue-author@example.com",
  "name": "QueueAuthor",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Create an article
# @name queueArticle
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Article pour la queue",
  "content": "Contenu de test"
}

### Submit it (-> SUBMITTED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{queueArticle.response.body.$.id}}/submit

### Create the "reviewer" account (replaces the current cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "queue-reviewer@example.com",
  "name": "QueueReviewer",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Article shows up in the reviewer's queue
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/submitted

### They review it
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{queueArticle.response.body.$.id}}/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "comment": "ok"
}

### Article drops out of their queue (already reviewed by them)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/submitted

### Log back in as the author (replaces the reviewer's cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "queue-author@example.com",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Author never sees their own article in the queue
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/submitted

### No auth (401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/submitted

### ==========================================================
### FRONT RECONCILIATION: article thumbnail, reuses the Day 19
### upload system (like the Day 20 avatar). Multipart uploads
### are a pain to script in .http, see the Day 19 note for the
### reference curl. Once you've got an uploadId:
### ==========================================================

### Create an account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "miniature@example.com",
  "name": "Miniature",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Create an article WITHOUT a thumbnail (default miniatureUrl expected)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Article sans miniature",
  "content": "Contenu de test"
}

### Create an article WITH a thumbnail (200, miniatureUrl = /api/uploads/<id>,
### and the upload flips to PUBLIC)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Article avec miniature",
  "content": "Contenu de test",
  "miniatureId": "REMPLACER_PAR_UN_ID_REEL"
}

### Use another account's PRIVATE upload as thumbnail (403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Vol de miniature",
  "content": "Contenu de test",
  "miniatureId": "REMPLACER_PAR_L_ID_D_UN_UPLOAD_D_UN_AUTRE_COMPTE"
}

### Use a PDF as thumbnail (400, not an image)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Miniature invalide",
  "content": "Contenu de test",
  "miniatureId": "REMPLACER_PAR_UN_ID_DE_PDF"
}

### ==========================================================
### GET /articles/mine (sorted by status) + visibility at
### upload time (for inline images in an article's content).
### ==========================================================

### Create an account
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mine@example.com",
  "name": "Mine",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Create a DRAFT
# @name mineDraft
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "My draft",
  "content": "c"
}

### Create a second article and submit it
# @name mineSubmitted
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "My submit",
  "content": "c"
}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/{{mineSubmitted.response.body.$.id}}/submit

### All your articles, whatever the status (2 expected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/mine

### DRAFTs only (1 expected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/mine?status=DRAFT

### Create a "third party" account (replaces the current cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "mine-other@example.com",
  "name": "MineOther",
  "password": "motdepasse123"
}

### Third party has no articles of their own (0, never the first account's)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/mine

### No auth (401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/articles/mine

### Upload straight as PUBLIC (for an inline image):
###
### curl -b cookies.txt -X POST http://localhost:4000/api/uploads \
###   -F "file=@myimage.png;type=image/png" \
###   -F "visibility=PUBLIC"
### -> 201, "visibility": "PUBLIC" right away, anyone can
### view it from the start, no linking route needed.
###
### Garbage or missing value falls back to "PRIVATE" (default
### unchanged):
### curl -b cookies.txt -X POST http://localhost:4000/api/uploads \
###   -F "file=@myimage.png;type=image/png" -F "visibility=whatever"

### ==========================================================
### DAY 22: dashboard (article/review counts per status +
### approval rate + account age). Covers the "User activity
### analytics and insights dashboard" module (Minor, +1) we'd missed.
